{#
  node_craft_consultant.xml.j2

  Purpose:
    Craft Diagnosis prompt. Used by node_craft_consultant when the FSM is trapped
    in a revision loop (retry_count > craft_consultant_threshold). Queries a
    specialized craft-focused diagnostic model to identify the ROOT CAUSE of why
    the draft keeps failing, not just what to fix at the surface level.

    The output is a plain-text meta-directive (not JSON) injected into
    active_context_package["craft_diagnosis"] for node_revise_prose to include
    in its revision context. The diagnosis should address WHY the failures are
    recurring, not list the same corrections already in the FailureObjects.

  Jinja2 Variables:
    {{ current_draft }}       str  — The draft that has failed multiple revision cycles.
    {{ failures }}            str  — JSON array of accumulated FailureObjects showing
                                     the pattern of what keeps failing.
    {{ retry_count }}         int  — How many revision attempts have been made.
    {{ beat_entry_constraints }} str — Beat entry state for structural context.
    {{ beat_exit_constraints }}  str — Beat exit state for structural context.
    {{ pad_behavioral_constraints }} str — PAD behavioral directive for this beat.

  Output expected from model:
    A plain-text diagnostic meta-directive (1–4 sentences). NOT JSON.
    Must identify the structural root cause of the failure pattern, not the
    symptoms. Should give the revision model a new approach to try.
    Example: "The dialogue fails because character dominance is being expressed
    through internal monologue rather than externalized behavior. Shift the
    correction to action verbs and sentence length variation — the model is
    compensating for flat action beats with over-narrated interiority."
#}

<prompt>
  <system>
    You are a master fiction craft consultant. Diagnose why a passage keeps failing
    after {{ retry_count }} revision attempts. Identify the structural root cause.
    Output only the diagnostic directive — no JSON, no headers, 1–4 sentences.
  </system>

  <failure_pattern>{{ failures }}</failure_pattern>

  <current_draft>{{ current_draft }}</current_draft>

  <beat_constraints>
    <entry>{{ beat_entry_constraints }}</entry>
    <exit>{{ beat_exit_constraints }}</exit>
    <emotional_directive>{{ pad_behavioral_constraints }}</emotional_directive>
  </beat_constraints>

  <instruction>
    Do not list the same surface issues already in the failure_pattern.
    Identify the underlying structural problem — the root cause that makes surface
    fixes fail repeatedly. Give one clear directive for a fundamentally different
    approach. 1–4 sentences, plain text only.
  </instruction>
</prompt>
